</addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBA CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANDA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, KAORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANDA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANDA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Pairs of coils (18) are fabricated by winding a wire in core slots (15) of an armature core (12). If the coil ends of each coil are formed into predetermined shapes by shaping winding, the winding at the coil ends of the coil wound in each core slot (15) is nearer to the end faces of the armature coil (12) toward the radial outside of the shaft (11). If the coil ends of each coil is formed by both shaping winding and direct winding, the wire is wound by shaping winding from the first turn to predetermined number of turns and then wound by direct winding for the rest of the turns at the coil ends.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Pour fabriquer des paires de bobines (18), on enroule un fil dans des fentes (15) d'un noyau d'induit (12). Si, pour façonner les extrémités de chaque bobine de manière prédéterminée, au niveau des extrémités de la bobine, on fait intervenir un enroulement de façonnage, au niveau des extrémités de la bobine, l'enroulement enroulé dans chaque fente (1) se trouve plus près des faces d'extrémité de la bobine d'armature (12), orienté radialement vers l'extérieur de l'arbre (11). Si, pour façonner les extrémités de chaque bobine, on fait appel à un enroulement de façonnage et à un enroulement direct, on enroule le fil en utilisant l'enroulement de façonnage depuis le premier tour jusqu'à un nombre prédéterminé de tours, puis on utilise l'enroulement direct pendant les tours restants au niveau des extrémités de bobine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>